{"skill":{"slug":"openclaw-claude-code","displayName":"Claude Code Agent"},"version":{"version":"0.3.0","createdAt":1771076231208,"changelog":"Major update with comprehensive documentation and advanced features.\n\n- Added full SKILL.md guide covering installation, usage, command reference, and advanced options.\n- Detailed instructions for managing persistent sessions, direct tool calls, and agent teams.\n- Descriptions of permission modes, tool whitelisting, and contextual session management.\n- Included examples for batch operations, session search/history, and agent collaboration.\n- Clarified multi-model support and custom configuration for expert users.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":7085,"sha256":"b214f5ac77e18b15dff6d2e35ba7e6657ceafe1f3841642eb0ae74e87ab12b6f","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":12327,"sha256":"4ff1e7e73494a903fc0ba018e2dfbd7ca0889ed559d5ec973842d50d39960bd3","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"examples/basic-mcp.ts","size":1420,"sha256":"49e9dba56c9bbc9470b55693bb44e31846343d349dbaef0668e0adc0f7f9fe07","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"examples/chat-store.ts","size":3656,"sha256":"35c05da49127ab0ed9fbd07744608bdb59ed7022144016fb1e3d0a41986feeb7","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"mcp_config.example.json","size":648,"sha256":"ffacbfab2965102122fcda24abcdca3ca644e85a6ad5e5c2cdf9741daab67829","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"package.json","size":679,"sha256":"f3a213ccd2ad0b4c38cfc5c7d30211bfb5bcb6f9fb72e1efca486bceb6221ca0","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/index.ts","size":24414,"sha256":"0200efbfa58031d9993c51fcf81264b7f7d66c2c7759355f3ccecb30a6c2fb4a","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/mcp/actions.ts","size":9606,"sha256":"7107bed432cda01b1007f1e094cdf2b1ec96043bfbd3f813b0f368822d6aaf3a","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/mcp/client.ts","size":1434,"sha256":"c26df91f0e03175362c312ec4361d85c98fee03add9c2ed7981dd414f33c3708","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/mcp/index.ts","size":189,"sha256":"93dfd7f618ca98b97af4456aafcbcc6682201a282e15cd6a601406cbf08e322a","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/mcp/logger.ts","size":1244,"sha256":"0a9b27776456cdca836cae5916f8e9c64974fbbe4bb284ffccbfc3a49421ed13","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/mcp/types.ts","size":3315,"sha256":"b4a12e82a67945191274459741f00cb1efcc429ccbeac99e31aec9af889346dd","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/mcp/utils.ts","size":477,"sha256":"8e1f055c7a00217c1e757f76146d03c392374e2c0f28e1817fc5e02ba84de577","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/store/index.ts","size":148,"sha256":"8d8add7be88932940adf284b18dbd298b0da84c656eeb588b525e6abe7ac9b94","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/store/indexeddb-storage.ts","size":1638,"sha256":"9ada27cf537a6cfeadbe31fed4373251693fddf11e784ff2c29dde566fa4ea36","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/store/persist.ts","size":2270,"sha256":"2af2ca3c293afbef497bd00c14d00ad34853d363072072480bee6487b197cbee","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/store/sync.ts","size":3215,"sha256":"2fd446360ab3b14727bc6318f2a2306148825f2e05ca488f2b48f855e8f3c128","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"tsconfig.json","size":399,"sha256":"473cf46753e92843a8663913427c0f1702f5244735352c95c8f0f3b0d2c0eb2e","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2563,"sha256":"0954b835015fdedeb6391d968e47b24bd2dbe7c7d7ed4235f50a3f09e6c185bf","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789067655879,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"f08973500d7081e70d43598c5011b32c9666fb3a9d72f6c42844925f0b2ab695","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/f08973500d7081e70d43598c5011b32c9666fb3a9d72f6c42844925f0b2ab695","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: openclaw-claude-code\nVersion: 0.3.0\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious due to its extensive high-risk capabilities, which, while potentially necessary for its stated purpose, could be leveraged for malicious activities if misused or compromised. Key indicators include the ability to execute arbitrary shell commands (`claude-code-skill bash <command>`) and launch arbitrary processes via MCP servers (`src/mcp/client.ts`, `mcp_config.example.json`), arbitrary file system read/write access (`read`, `Write` tools in `src/index.ts`), and the option to bypass security permissions (`--skip-permissions` in `src/index.ts`, `bypassPermissions` mode in `SKILL.md`). Furthermore, the `--base-url` option allows the agent to connect to arbitrary external API endpoints, enabling potential data exfiltration or unauthorized actions if directed to a malicious server, as documented in `SKILL.md` and `README.md`.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779163988986},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":30,"checkedAt":1789067655879},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a disclosed Claude Code control tool, but it grants broad command, file, tool, backend, and MCP subprocess authority with weak guardrails.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The CLI sends prompts, commands, paths, tool arguments, session data, and configuration to a configurable backend URL without enforcing HTTPS or authentication for remote endpoints. MCP subprocesses also inherit the full parent environment.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill itself installs as a Node CLI from a local path and has no package lifecycle script hooks, but dependencies are semver ranges and the example MCP configuration uses npx -y with unpinned MCP packages.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The documentation discloses powerful controls, but defaults and examples normalize auto-accepted edits, tool auto-approval, broad Bash/Read/Edit/Write use, and permission bypass modes without strong user-facing containment or confirmation guidance.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Persistent sessions, session history, local store examples, and MCP server configuration are expected for the purpose, but MCP config writes can persist plaintext token fields and the config path is changeable by exported API.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The advertised purpose matches much of the implementation: it exposes Claude Code/MCP-style command execution, file reads/writes, code search, persistent sessions, and arbitrary tool calls. Those capabilities are high impact, and the CLI includes generic tool dispatch plus direct Bash and Write examples.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review this carefully before installing. Use only in trusted, isolated project directories; prefer plan/default permission modes; avoid skip-permissions and bypassPermissions; restrict allowed tools to the minimum needed; use only authenticated local or trusted HTTPS backends; do not put real tokens in MCP JSON configs; pin MCP server packages instead of npx -y floating versions; and run third-party MCP servers with a minimal environment.","findings":"[TP4] unexpected: Downgraded: the scanner compared the description to store helper files, but the package also contains a CLI and MCP modules that do implement the declared Claude Code control purpose.\n[AS2] expected: Reading and updating an MCP config file is expected for an MCP management package, but it is still sensitive because configs can include commands, server definitions, and token-bearing env fields.\n[P3] expected: The cited 'Send message to a persistent session' text is ordinary session functionality, not artifact-backed prompt injection or covert exfiltration.\n[E1] expected: External model/backend examples are disclosed proxy functionality, but users should treat any nonlocal endpoint as receiving task prompts and control data.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: Accepted in part: command execution, writes, auto-approval, skip-permissions, and bypassPermissions are purpose-aligned but under-scoped and under-warned for such high-impact authority.\n[EA1] unexpected: Accepted: the generic call command can invoke any named Claude Code tool with caller-provided JSON, expanding beyond safer dedicated subcommands.\n[EA2] unexpected: Accepted: auto-approval and permissive permission modes are disclosed, but they materially reduce human oversight over shell and file operations.\n[SC1] unexpected: Low-weight concern: package dependencies use version ranges and no lockfile was present, increasing supply-chain drift risk but not showing malicious behavior.\n[T09] unexpected: Accepted: the configurable backend URL does not enforce HTTPS or backend authentication for remote hosts, and MCP credentials may be stored in plaintext JSON config.\n[T05] unexpected: Accepted: configured MCP subprocesses inherit nearly the entire parent environment, which can expose unrelated credentials to third-party server processes.\n[T08] unexpected: Accepted: the example configuration launches unpinned MCP packages through npx -y, which can download and execute changed package code at runtime.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789067655879}}}}}